    rdf:value """Wednesday, January 12, 1916, I Tatti
Julia, Geoffrey
Splendid weather 
(5 lunch, 3 dinner)
No cook but Amerigo managed somehow.  I went in to the Carrels, taking Mrs. Ross to call on Miss Murray, and we then called for Miss Prestley whom I brought back to lunch. We had a glorious walk over the down for S. Clemente .  Geoffrey had just heard that Marcella Michela has scarlet fever. He is sure to have caught it. It is a great disappointment. He called there and left flowers and a note, and then went to the Casa di Cura."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 18 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1916> .

